anv: report scratch BO allocation failure at shader creation

anv_scratch_pool_alloc() returns NULL when the scratch BO cannot be
allocated (a TODO since the pool was written).  Shader state emission
ignored that: on Gfx9-12 the NULL BO became ScratchSpaceBasePointer 0, so
vkCreate*Pipelines returned VK_SUCCESS and the shader's scratch accesses
went to address 0.  On Gfx12.5+, anv_scratch_pool_get_surf() and
anv_shader_get_scratch_surf() dereferenced or relocated the NULL BO.

Scratch BOs are cached per size bucket and stage for the lifetime of the
device, so reserve them in anv_shader_create() and fail creation with
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY.  The lookups made while emitting state then
cannot fail.  Command-time paths and internal simple shaders mark the batch
as failed instead of programming a NULL BO.

Tested on HD 620 (KBL GT2) with an LD_PRELOAD shim that fails the 42 MiB
scratch GEM_CREATE: pipeline creation now returns
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY instead of VK_SUCCESS, and the same shader
still dispatches correctly when the allocation succeeds.

